---
description: Frontend scale — container-type, cqw/cqh, cq-responsive mixin.
globs: frontend/**/*.{tsx,scss}
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use `container-type: size` on the shells that should define cqw/cqh (`app-container`, `app-content`, `view-container`, etc.).
- `cq-responsive` in `mixins.scss`: unitless numbers → portrait **cqw**, landscape **cqh**. No other modes — if you need different mapping, write cqw/cqh by hand.
- Don’t `@include cq-responsive` inside `.is-portrait &` / `.is-landscape &` (breaks selectors).
- Skip the mixin when numbers or units differ per orientation, or when you want a fixed axis (e.g. both max dimensions in cqw only).
